    {
      "id": "claim_04b1022dd7d8451e89a480385b340a66",
      "statement": "delete_course (hard delete path, draft courses only) iterates a course's files and calls seaweedfs.delete_file, but only logs a warning on failure instead of aborting, so SeaweedFS unavailability can leave orphaned blobs on the filer while the corresponding DB rows are still removed; load_data_node raises and fails the whole course-generation run if it cannot load any source file from SeaweedFS, making SeaweedFS availability a hard dependency for course generation.",
